# The checkout is on Windows; the things it produces run on Linux. Deploys go
# out from WSL2, which reads this same working tree through /mnt/c.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is false here today, so this changes nothing right now. It
# exists so that a clone on a machine where it is *true* does not silently
# produce a deploy.sh that dies with `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`, or systemd
# units and a Caddyfile carrying carriage returns.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh          text eol=lf
*.service     text eol=lf
*.timer       text eol=lf
Caddyfile*    text eol=lf

# Binary, and never to be line-ending-converted or diffed as text.
*.png         binary
*.ico         binary
*.db          binary
